# Build context for the Jetson transcription image
# (jetson/docker-compose.example.yml, `context: .`).
#
# This image only copies `requirements.txt` and `server.py`, so the ignore file
# is cheap insurance rather than a fix for a live leak — but the compose file in
# this directory carries TRANSCRIPTION_API_KEY, and the build context is sent to
# the daemon whole regardless of what the Dockerfile ends up copying.
#
# Pinned by server/tests/test_dockerfile_contract.py (issue #234).

# Secrets and local config
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yml.*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests
test_server.py
conftest.py

# Caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Documentation and repo metadata
*.md
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
